# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D guide ended by mentioning that local encodings are needed when working with two dimensions. This guide takes that step, for the **two-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model on a square lattice**, using the **Verstraete-Cirac (VC) encoding** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"
msgstr "Panduan 1D diakhiri dengan menyebut bahwa encoding lokal dibutuhkan saat bekerja dengan dua dimensi. Panduan ini mengambil langkah itu, untuk **model Fermi-Hubbard dua dimensi pada kisi persegi**, memakai **encoding Verstraete-Cirac (VC)** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are three differences from the 1D problem, forming the basis of this work:\n"
msgstr "Ada tiga perbedaan dari masalah 1D, yang menjadi dasar pekerjaan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The flow sets multiply.** A chain has two arrow orientations; a square lattice has four (east, west, north, south), and each is a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths (one per lattice row or column) rather than a single path.\n"
msgstr "**Flow set bertambah banyak.** Sebuah rantai punya dua orientasi panah; kisi persegi punya empat (east, west, north, south), dan masing-masing adalah gabungan lintasan berarah yang saling lepas titik-sudutnya (satu per baris atau kolom kisi), bukan satu lintasan tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoding gains an ancilla per site**, not one for the whole system, giving a\n"
msgstr "## **Encoding mendapat satu ancilla per site**, bukan satu untuk seluruh sistem, sehingga menghasilkan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$. Transfer operators become weight-3 (horizontal) and weight-4 (vertical) Paulis, and each of the four flow sets maps to its own Pauli shape, so each needs its own diagonalizing Clifford.\n"
msgstr "    rasio qubit-ke-mode sebesar $2$. Operator transfer menjadi Pauli berbobot 3 (horizontal) dan berbobot 4 (vertikal), dan tiap dari empat flow set dipetakan ke bentuk Pauli-nya sendiri, jadi masing-masing butuh Clifford pendiagonal sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a subspace**: the joint $+1$\n"
msgstr "## **Hamiltonian ter-encode hanya faithful pada sebuah subruang**: eigenspace gabungan $+1$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    eigenspace of the plaquette constraints that every 2D local encoding carries <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). In 1D the encoding was a plain isometry and the verification was a spectrum check. Here, the comparison has to be projected, as [step 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers) illustrates.\n"
msgstr "    dari batasan plaquette yang dibawa setiap encoding lokal 2D <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). Di 1D, encoding-nya adalah isometri biasa dan verifikasinya berupa pemeriksaan spektrum. Di sini, perbandingannya harus diproyeksikan, seperti diilustrasikan [langkah 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is the same shape as in 1D: the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step becomes constant in the lattice size, at $24$ ($16$ for the hopping, matching Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), plus $8$ for the interaction), while a term-by-term Trotterization of the same encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly. The gate count still grows with the number of bonds, of course; what becomes size-independent is how many layers those gates occupy. Depths throughout are counted on an abstract, fully connected register; mapping the encoding onto a device’s restricted coupling map is its own problem, which is discussed at the end.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya berbentuk sama seperti di 1D: depth dua-qubit satu langkah Trotter menjadi konstan terhadap ukuran kisi, di $24$ ($16$ untuk hopping, sesuai Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), ditambah $8$ untuk interaksi), sementara Trotterisasi suku demi suku dari Hamiltonian ter-encode yang sama tumbuh linear. Jumlah gate tentu saja tetap tumbuh seiring jumlah ikatan; yang menjadi tidak bergantung pada ukuran adalah berapa banyak layer yang ditempati gate-gate itu. Depth di seluruh bagian dihitung pada register abstrak yang terhubung penuh; memetakan encoding ke coupling map perangkat yang terbatas adalah masalah tersendiri, yang dibahas di bagian akhir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The lattice and its four orientations {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"
msgstr "Kisi dan empat orientasinya {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first change is visible on the directed interaction graph. Sites are numbered in row-major order, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, and every bond carries both orientations, as the chain did in 1D, but now the bonds run along two axes:\n"
msgstr "Perubahan pertama terlihat pada graf interaksi berarah. Site dinomori dalam urutan row-major, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, dan setiap ikatan membawa kedua orientasi, seperti pada rantai di 1D, tetapi sekarang ikatannya berjalan sepanjang dua sumbu:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The commutation rule is the 1D one, unchanged: two transfer operators sharing a site **commute** when the arrows flow through it and **anticommute** when they clash. However, a site now has up to four incident bonds rather than two, so the arrows through it can clash in more ways, and a set of arrows that never clashes is no longer a single path. Reading the horizontal arrows left-to-right gives one such set, the vertical arrows from top-to-bottom gives another, and reversing each gives two more. These are the east, west, north, and south flow sets that organize everything that follows.\n"
msgstr "Aturan komutasinya sama dengan di 1D, tidak berubah: dua operator transfer yang berbagi satu site **komut** ketika panah mengalir melaluinya dan **antikomut** ketika bertabrakan. Namun, sebuah site sekarang punya hingga empat ikatan, bukan dua, jadi panah yang melaluinya bisa bertabrakan dengan lebih banyak cara, dan himpunan panah yang tidak pernah bertabrakan tidak lagi berupa satu lintasan. Membaca panah horizontal dari kiri ke kanan memberi satu himpunan semacam itu, panah vertikal dari atas ke bawah memberi satu lagi, dan membalik masing-masing memberi dua lagi. Inilah flow set east, west, north, dan south yang mengorganisasi semua yang menyusul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Verstraete-Cirac encoding {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"
msgstr "Encoding Verstraete-Cirac {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verstraete-Cirac (VC) pairs every fermionic mode $j$ with its own auxiliary qubit. With $N$ lattice sites, mode $j$ lives on qubit $j$ and its ancilla is on qubit $N + j$, so the register holds $2N$ qubits. Vertex operators stay as simple as they can be,\n"
msgstr "Verstraete-Cirac (VC) memasangkan setiap mode fermionik $j$ dengan qubit bantunya sendiri. Dengan $N$ site kisi, mode $j$ berada di qubit $j$ dan ancilla-nya di qubit $N + j$, sehingga register berisi $2N$ qubit. Operator vertex tetap sesederhana mungkin,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what makes the occupations directly readable later. Transfer operators depend on the edge orientation. For a horizontal edge $j \\to k$ with $j$ the western site, and a vertical edge with $j$ the northern site,\n"
msgstr "yang membuat okupansi bisa dibaca langsung nanti. Operator transfer bergantung pada orientasi sisi. Untuk sisi horizontal $j \\to k$ dengan $j$ sebagai site barat, dan sisi vertikal dengan $j$ sebagai site utara,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "a weight-3 “triangle” and a weight-4 “square”. Identifying each arrow matters: with $j$ as the western site, $j \\to k$ points east, but with $j$ as the northern site, it points south. The reverse orientations follow from the identity $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which turns the `XXZ` triangle into `YYZ`, and the `XYXY` square into `YXXY`. Those four distinct labels are the four flow sets, and the rest of this guide tracks them.\n"
msgstr "sebuah “segitiga” berbobot 3 dan sebuah “persegi” berbobot 4. Mengidentifikasi setiap panah itu penting: dengan $j$ sebagai site barat, $j \\to k$ menunjuk ke timur, tetapi dengan $j$ sebagai site utara, ia menunjuk ke selatan. Orientasi sebaliknya mengikuti dari identitas $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, yang mengubah segitiga `XXZ` menjadi `YYZ`, dan persegi `XYXY` menjadi `YXXY`. Keempat label berbeda itulah keempat flow set, dan sisa panduan ini melacaknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **These are not quite Eq. (A1) of Ref.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), which states “up to single-qubit rotations” and differs in three ways worth naming, since a reader checking the paper will notice:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Ini tidak persis sama dengan Pers. (A1) dari Ref.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), yang menyatakan “hingga rotasi single-qubit” dan berbeda dalam tiga hal yang perlu disebutkan, karena pembaca yang mencocokkan dengan makalahnya pasti akan menyadarinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The prefactor:** Eq. (A1) carries none. The $\\tfrac12$ here is what makes $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, matching the normalization $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ that [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") uses. The paper only ever needs its transfer operators inside $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, where a scale factor is absorbed into the rotation angle; here they have to be *operators* that satisfy an identity.\n"
msgstr "**Prefaktor:** Pers. (A1) tidak punya prefaktor. $\\tfrac12$ di sini membuat $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, sesuai dengan normalisasi $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ yang dipakai oleh [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Makalah itu hanya membutuhkan operator transfernya di dalam $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, di mana faktor skala terserap ke dalam sudut rotasi; di sini operator tersebut harus berupa *operator* yang memenuhi suatu identitas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Orientation:** Eq. (A1) selects letters by the row parity of $j$, which for a horizontal edge is the same for both endpoints, so it does not distinguish $T_{jk}$ from $T_{kj}$. The paper recovers the orientation separately, by conjugating with a layer of $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. This guide instead folds it into the encoding, deriving the reverse from $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which is what makes the two orientations land on different Paulis in step 3.\n"
msgstr "**Orientasi:** Pers. (A1) memilih huruf berdasarkan paritas baris $j$, yang untuk sisi horizontal sama untuk kedua ujungnya, jadi tidak membedakan $T_{jk}$ dari $T_{kj}$. Makalah itu memulihkan orientasi secara terpisah, dengan melakukan konjugasi memakai satu layer $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. Panduan ini justru memasukkannya ke dalam encoding, dengan menurunkan kebalikannya dari $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, yang membuat kedua orientasi jatuh ke Pauli yang berbeda di langkah 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **The vertical shape:** Eq. (A1) alternates `XXXX` and `YYYY` by row parity, where this guide uses a single `XYXY`. These are two ways of getting the same thing: a letter asymmetry that makes a vertical edge clash correctly with the horizontal edges meeting it. Do not read the difference as a free basis choice. Dropping the parity alternation and using a single `XXXX` breaks the algebra outright, which is why the distinct letters are checked rather than assumed.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Bentuk vertikal:** Pers. (A1) bergantian antara `XXXX` dan `YYYY` menurut paritas baris, sedangkan panduan ini memakai satu `XYXY`. Keduanya adalah dua cara untuk mendapatkan hal yang sama: asimetri huruf yang membuat sisi vertikal berbenturan dengan benar terhadap sisi horizontal yang bertemu dengannya. Jangan anggap perbedaan ini sebagai pilihan basis yang bebas. Menghilangkan pergantian paritas dan memakai satu `XXXX` saja langsung merusak aljabarnya, makanya huruf-huruf yang berbeda itu diperiksa, bukan sekadar diasumsikan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The ancilla is attached to a *site*, giving the ratio $2$; it is the Derby-Klassen encoding that places an auxiliary qubit per (odd) plaquette, for the smaller ratio $3/2$. VC is used here because its transfer operators are the ones whose diagonalizing Cliffords Ref.   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives in closed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ancilla dipasang pada sebuah *site*, sehingga rasionya $2$; encoding Derby-Klassen-lah yang menaruh satu qubit tambahan per plakuet (ganjil), untuk rasio yang lebih kecil, $3/2$. VC dipakai di sini karena operator transfernya adalah operator yang Clifford pendiagonalnya diberikan dalam bentuk tertutup oleh Ref.   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian on a square lattice {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian pada kisi persegi {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The construction is the same as in 1D, but with a two-dimensional edge list. Sites keep the row-major numbering used for the figure above, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, so that horizontal bonds connect consecutive indices, and vertical bonds connect indices differing by `cols`:\n"
msgstr "Konstruksinya sama seperti di 1D, tetapi dengan daftar sisi dua dimensi. Site tetap memakai penomoran row-major seperti pada gambar di atas, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, sehingga ikatan horizontal menghubungkan indeks berurutan, dan ikatan vertikal menghubungkan indeks yang selisihnya `cols`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"four-flow-sets-instead-of-two\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Four flow sets instead of two {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"
msgstr "2. Empat flow set, bukan dua {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each hopping term is classified by the direction its arrow points on the lattice. Comparing the `divmod` row/column coordinates of the two endpoints separates horizontal from vertical edges, and the sign of the difference picks the orientation. Everything diagonal (the identity, the $V_j$ and the $V_j V_k$ terms) goes into a fifth group:\n"
msgstr "Setiap suku hopping diklasifikasikan menurut arah panah-nya pada kisi. Membandingkan koordinat baris/kolom `divmod` dari kedua ujungnya memisahkan sisi horizontal dari vertikal, dan tanda selisihnya menentukan orientasi. Semua yang diagonal (identitas, suku $V_j$ dan $V_j V_k$) masuk ke kelompok kelima:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Orientation convention.** The names are simply read off the figure above: an arrow is **east** or **west** as it points right or left along a row, and **north** or **south** as it points up or down a column. Since the numbering runs row-major, east and south are the index-increasing directions. Nothing downstream depends on the names (they only label groups), but they are easy to confuse, so it is worth fixing them against the picture. Ref.   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) names its square-lattice flow sets the same way.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Konvensi orientasi.** Nama-namanya diambil begitu saja dari gambar di atas: sebuah panah disebut **east** atau **west** kalau mengarah ke kanan atau kiri sepanjang baris, dan **north** atau **south** kalau mengarah ke atas atau bawah sepanjang kolom. Karena penomoran berjalan row-major, east dan south adalah arah dengan indeks yang bertambah. Tidak ada yang bergantung pada nama-nama ini di langkah berikutnya (hanya label kelompok), tetapi gampang tertukar, jadi sebaiknya dipastikan lewat gambar. Ref.   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) menamai flow set kisi persegi miliknya dengan cara yang sama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Within one flow set every arrow either meets another head-to-tail or does not meet it at all, as in 1D, so a flow set still commutes term-by-term and its evolution carries no Trotter error. What is new is that a flow set is now disconnected: the east set of a `rows x cols` lattice consists of `rows` independent left-to-right paths. That disconnection is a gift rather than a complication, as step 6 shows.\n"
msgstr "Dalam satu flow set, setiap panah entah bertemu panah lain secara head-to-tail atau tidak bertemu sama sekali, seperti di 1D, jadi flow set tetap komut suku demi suku dan evolusinya tidak membawa error Trotter. Yang baru adalah bahwa flow set sekarang tidak terhubung: set east pada kisi `rows x cols` terdiri dari `rows` lintasan kiri-ke-kanan yang saling independen. Keterputusan itu justru keuntungan, bukan komplikasi, seperti yang ditunjukkan langkah 6.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"encode-the-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encode the operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"
msgstr "3. Meng-encode operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is one function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string, which is handed to [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Compared with the 1D version, the body has more cases: diagonal, horizontal, vertical, and the reverse orientations through $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"
msgstr "Encoding-nya berupa satu fungsi yang memetakan satu operator transfer umum menjadi sebuah string Pauli, yang lalu diteruskan ke [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Dibandingkan versi 1D, isinya punya lebih banyak kasus: diagonal, horizontal, vertikal, dan orientasi kebalikan lewat $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one problem. [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") calls back with a generator and nothing else, while deciding a bond’s Pauli string also needs `cols` to recover row and column coordinates from a mode index. Rather than nest the functions to close over it, [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial) binds it, which keeps both functions at the top level and independently callable.\n"
msgstr "Ada satu masalah. [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") memanggil balik hanya dengan sebuah generator dan tidak ada yang lain, padahal menentukan string Pauli sebuah ikatan juga membutuhkan `cols` untuk memulihkan koordinat baris dan kolom dari indeks mode. Daripada menyarangkan fungsi untuk menangkapnya, [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial) mengikatnya, sehingga kedua fungsi tetap berada di level teratas dan bisa dipanggil secara independen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The point of grouping before mapping can be seen immediately: each flow set encodes to a single Pauli shape, uniform across the whole set.\n"
msgstr "Manfaat mengelompokkan sebelum memetakan langsung terlihat: setiap flow set di-encode menjadi satu bentuk Pauli, seragam di seluruh set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping shapes are distinct, so each flow set gets its own Clifford in [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). The reverse orientations are different Paulis, not the same ones relabeled; this is why a 2D flow-set synthesis needs four circuits, where the 1D synthesis needs one.\n"
msgstr "Keempat bentuk hopping itu berbeda, jadi setiap flow set mendapat Clifford-nya sendiri di [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). Orientasi kebalikan adalah Pauli yang berbeda, bukan Pauli yang sama dengan label lain; inilah sebabnya sintesis flow set 2D membutuhkan empat circuit, sedangkan sintesis 1D hanya butuh satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Transpile with the custom encoding {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "4. Transpile dengan encoding kustom {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This stage is the 1D one with a wider qubit register: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") maps the $N$-mode register onto $2N$ qubits, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") carries the encoding, and its `product_formula` argument selects how the resulting [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) is decomposed. Compare [step 6 of the 1D guide](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), which builds the same pipeline for a single ancilla.\n"
msgstr "Tahap ini sama seperti yang 1D dengan register qubit yang lebih lebar: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") memetakan register $N$ mode ke $2N$ qubit, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") membawa encoding-nya, dan argumen `product_formula`-nya memilih bagaimana [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) yang dihasilkan didekomposisi. Bandingkan dengan [langkah 6 pada panduan 1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), yang membangun pipeline yang sama untuk satu ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Five gates, carrying the 6, 6, 6, 6, and 22 terms counted in step 2. Each is mapped and synthesized independently, so the partition decided at the fermionic level survives all the way into the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Lima gate, yang membawa 6, 6, 6, 6, dan 22 suku seperti dihitung di langkah 2. Masing-masing dipetakan dan disintesis secara independen, jadi partisi yang ditentukan di level fermionik bertahan sampai ke dalam circuit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the baseline: the encoding and the grouping are both in place, but [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) synthesizes each flow set term by term, and the depth grows with the lattice.\n"
msgstr "Itulah baseline-nya: encoding dan pengelompokan sudah terpasang, tetapi [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) mensintesis setiap flow set suku demi suku, dan depth-nya tumbuh seiring ukuran kisi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. A depth-2 Clifford per flow set {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"
msgstr "5. Clifford berdepth 2 per flow set {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mechanism is the same as in 1D: conjugate a whole commuting flow set by a Clifford that maps each of its terms to a distinct weight-1 Pauli, so that the evolution of the entire set costs only single-qubit rotations. In 1D, one brickwork of `CZ` gates did this.\n"
msgstr "Mekanismenya sama seperti di 1D: lakukan konjugasi satu flow set komut penuh dengan sebuah Clifford yang memetakan setiap sukunya ke Pauli berbobot 1 yang berbeda, sehingga evolusi seluruh set hanya memerlukan rotasi single-qubit. Di 1D, satu brickwork gate `CZ` melakukan ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In 2D, each flow set needs its own circuit, following Section IV C and Fig. 7 of Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). All four act on one line of the lattice at a time (a row for east/west, a column for north/south) together with that line’s ancillas, and all four have the same three-part shape:\n"
msgstr "Di 2D, setiap flow set butuh circuit-nya sendiri, mengikuti Bagian IV C dan Gambar 7 dari Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). Keempatnya bekerja pada satu garis kisi sekali waktu (satu baris untuk east/west, satu kolom untuk north/south) bersama ancilla garis itu, dan keempatnya punya bentuk tiga bagian yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A layer of single-qubit rotations, putting each qubit in the basis its flow set needs.\n"
msgstr "Satu layer rotasi single-qubit, yang menempatkan setiap qubit pada basis yang dibutuhkan flow set-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A first `CX` layer, always site-to-ancilla on the same site.\n"
msgstr "Layer `CX` pertama, selalu dari site ke ancilla pada site yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A second `CX` layer, coupling neighbors along the line.\n"
msgstr "Layer `CX` kedua, yang mengaitkan tetangga di sepanjang garis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2 and 3 are the only two-qubit layers, so the two-qubit depth is $2$, regardless of how long the line is. They are written out one function per flow set below. The rotations are what they are because they were found, by conjugating each flow set’s terms and requiring distinct weight-1 images, so treat them as given and rely on the check that follows.\n"
msgstr "Langkah 2 dan 3 adalah satu-satunya layer dua-qubit, jadi depth dua-qubit-nya $2$, berapa pun panjang garisnya. Semuanya ditulis satu fungsi per flow set di bawah ini. Rotasinya seperti itu karena ditemukan dengan melakukan konjugasi pada suku-suku tiap flow set dan mensyaratkan citra berbobot 1 yang berbeda, jadi anggap saja sebagai yang sudah diberikan dan andalkan pemeriksaan yang menyusul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two horizontal sets are the simplest. Their terms are weight-3, `XXZ` and `YYZ`, and differ only by the extra $S$ that turns $X$ into $Y$ on the sites:\n"
msgstr "Dua set horizontal adalah yang paling sederhana. Suku-sukunya berbobot 3, `XXZ` dan `YYZ`, dan hanya berbeda oleh $S$ ekstra yang mengubah $X$ menjadi $Y$ pada site:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two vertical sets are weight-4, `XYXY` and `YXXY`, and are correspondingly busier: the rotations alternate with the position along the line, and the second `CX` layer alternates too, coupling sites on even positions and ancillas on odd ones (or the reverse):\n"
msgstr "Dua set vertikal berbobot 4, `XYXY` dan `YXXY`, dan sesuai dengan itu lebih ramai: rotasinya berganti-ganti menurut posisi di sepanjang garis, dan layer `CX` kedua juga berganti-ganti, mengaitkan site pada posisi genap dan ancilla pada posisi ganjil (atau sebaliknya):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drawn on a single three-site line (its sites first, then their ancillas) the whole mechanism fits in one picture. The triangle shape is the clearer of the two: a basis change on the ancillas, then two `CX` layers, the first pairs each site with its own ancilla and the second reaches to the next site along the line.\n"
msgstr "Digambar pada satu garis tiga site (site-nya dulu, lalu ancilla-nya) seluruh mekanismenya muat dalam satu gambar. Bentuk segitiga adalah yang lebih jelas dari keduanya: perubahan basis pada ancilla, lalu dua layer `CX`, yang pertama memasangkan setiap site dengan ancilla-nya sendiri dan yang kedua menjangkau site berikutnya di sepanjang garis.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The square shape needs more single-qubit work (the rotations alternate along the line) and its second `CX` layer alternates between coupling sites and coupling ancillas:\n"
msgstr "Bentuk persegi membutuhkan lebih banyak kerja single-qubit (rotasinya berganti-ganti di sepanjang garis) dan layer `CX` keduanya berganti antara mengaitkan site dan mengaitkan ancilla:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are two `CX` layers deep, and adding sites to the line widens them without deepening them; that is the whole constant-depth claim, visible by inspection. The west and north Cliffords differ only in their single-qubit layers, so they are not drawn separately.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya sedalam dua layer `CX`, dan menambah site pada garis hanya melebarkannya tanpa memperdalamnya; itulah seluruh klaim depth konstan, terlihat langsung dengan pemeriksaan. Clifford west dan north hanya berbeda pada layer single-qubit-nya, jadi tidak digambar terpisah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the synthesis still needs is determining where each term ends up. A line of $L$ sites carries $L - 1$ bonds, each contributing one term, so the helper below returns one entry per bond: the qubit that the term landed on, and the single-qubit Pauli it became. Crucially, these are read off the conjugation rather than predicted. Unlike 1D, where one `CZ` brickwork maps $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ in closed form, there is no such formula here, and the ancillas of a column line are not contiguous. The only thing that differs between the flow sets is the Pauli string going in, which step 3 already printed:\n"
msgstr "Yang masih dibutuhkan sintesis adalah menentukan ke mana setiap suku berakhir. Sebuah garis dengan $L$ site punya $L - 1$ ikatan, masing-masing menyumbang satu suku, jadi helper di bawah mengembalikan satu entri per ikatan: qubit tempat suku itu mendarat, dan Pauli single-qubit yang ia jadi. Yang penting, ini dibaca dari konjugasi, bukan ditebak. Tidak seperti 1D, di mana satu brickwork `CZ` memetakan $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ dalam bentuk tertutup, di sini tidak ada rumus seperti itu, dan ancilla pada garis kolom tidak berurutan. Satu-satunya yang berbeda antar flow set adalah string Pauli yang masuk, yang sudah dicetak langkah 3:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The images must come out distinct and weight-1, so that each term can be rotated independently on its own qubit; the two-qubit depth of $2$ is already visible in the four constructions above, each emitting two `CX` layers irrespective of the line length. Below, both properties are checked across every flow set, every line, and several lattice sizes. Step 6 then calls `clifford_supports`, so it is a working part of the synthesis rather than only a demonstration.\n"
msgstr "Citra-citranya harus keluar berbeda dan berbobot 1, supaya setiap suku bisa dirotasi secara independen pada qubit-nya sendiri; depth dua-qubit $2$ sudah terlihat dalam empat konstruksi di atas, masing-masing menghasilkan dua layer `CX` terlepas dari panjang garis. Di bawah, kedua properti itu diperiksa pada setiap flow set, setiap garis, dan beberapa ukuran kisi. Langkah 6 lalu memanggil `clifford_supports`, jadi ini bagian kerja dari sintesis, bukan sekadar demonstrasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Flow-set-aware synthesis {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "6. Sintesis yang sadar flow set {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The synthesis gets a helpful head start. Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself group by group, `synthesize` is called once per flow set (five times here, four hopping sets plus the diagonal group) so every hopping term it sees shares one Pauli shape, and one Clifford diagonalizes all of them. It only has to read that shape off the first term and sort the rest by which line they sit on. Then comes the observation that makes two dimensions cheaper than one might fear:\n"
msgstr "Sintesis mendapat awalan yang menguntungkan. Karena [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") memecah dirinya sendiri kelompok demi kelompok, `synthesize` dipanggil sekali per flow set (lima kali di sini, empat set hopping plus kelompok diagonal) sehingga setiap suku hopping yang dilihatnya punya satu bentuk Pauli yang sama, dan satu Clifford mendiagonalkan semuanya. Ia hanya perlu membaca bentuk itu dari suku pertama dan mengurutkan sisanya menurut garis tempat mereka berada. Lalu muncul pengamatan yang membuat dua dimensi lebih murah daripada yang dikhawatirkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The components of a single flow set are vertex-disjoint: the west set’s rows share no qubits. So all of a flow set’s Cliffords can be emitted together and they share the same two two-qubit layers, rather than queueing up one row after another. A flow set therefore costs a fixed number of layers (two for the Clifford and two for its inverse) no matter how many rows or columns the lattice has, which is why the total depth ends up constant.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Komponen-komponen dari satu flow set saling vertex-disjoint: baris-baris set west tidak berbagi qubit. Jadi semua Clifford sebuah flow set bisa dikeluarkan bersamaan dan berbagi dua layer dua-qubit yang sama, bukan mengantre satu baris demi satu baris. Karena itu sebuah flow set memakan jumlah layer yang tetap (dua untuk Clifford dan dua untuk inversnya) berapa pun banyaknya baris atau kolom pada kisi, dan itulah sebabnya depth totalnya akhirnya konstan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in 1D, this is deliberately written for this encoding: it recognizes the four Pauli shapes and raises on anything else rather than falling back silently. It also assumes the one-flow-set-per-gate split above, and says so; more than one hopping shape in a single gate means the grouping was not applied, which is an error rather than something to work around.\n"
msgstr "Seperti di 1D, ini sengaja ditulis khusus untuk encoding ini: ia mengenali keempat bentuk Pauli dan melempar error pada yang lain, alih-alih diam-diam beralih ke cara lain. Ia juga mengasumsikan pemisahan satu-flow-set-per-gate di atas, dan menyatakannya; lebih dari satu bentuk hopping dalam satu gate berarti pengelompokan tidak diterapkan, yang merupakan error dan bukan sesuatu yang perlu disiasati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Like its 1D counterpart, this synthesis takes no number of Trotter steps. A Trotter step has to cycle *between* the flow sets, but `transpile_trotter_step` below decomposes the fermionic circuit into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per set, so this method only ever sees one set at a time and could only repeat *within* it, which changes nothing: repeating one operator just splits its own evolution into equal pieces.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Seperti padanan 1D-nya, sintesis ini tidak menerima jumlah langkah Trotter. Satu langkah Trotter harus bersiklus *di antara* flow set, tetapi `transpile_trotter_step` di bawah mendekomposisi circuit fermionik menjadi satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") per set, sehingga method ini hanya melihat satu set sekali waktu dan hanya bisa mengulang *di dalamnya*, yang tidak mengubah apa-apa: mengulang satu operator hanya membagi evolusinya sendiri menjadi bagian-bagian yang sama besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Multi-step Trotterization therefore needs a product formula that respects the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") inside a single gate, before the decomposition. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that, and [step 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) uses it to measure the convergence.\n"
msgstr "  Trotterisasi multi-langkah karena itu membutuhkan product formula yang menghormati [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") milik operator di dalam satu gate, sebelum dekomposisi. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") melakukannya, dan [langkah 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) memakainya untuk mengukur konvergensi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Note the two similarly named classes at play. Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter), used as the baseline above, acts on the *mapped* Hamiltonian, where the grouping is already gone. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the fermionic counterpart, and it is the one that can still see the flow sets.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Perhatikan dua kelas bernama mirip yang terlibat. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) milik Qiskit, yang dipakai sebagai baseline di atas, bekerja pada Hamiltonian yang sudah *dipetakan*, di mana pengelompokan sudah hilang. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") adalah padanan fermionik-nya, dan ia yang masih bisa melihat flow set.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-result-constant-depth\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. The result: constant depth {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"
msgstr "7. Hasilnya: depth konstan {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything so far ran on the single $3 \\times 3$ lattice built in step 1. Comparing the two synthesis paths across growing lattices needs that whole sequence (operator, grouping, encoding, circuit, pass manager) repeated per size, so it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Semua yang sejauh ini dijalankan memakai satu kisi $3 \\times 3$ yang dibangun di langkah 1. Membandingkan kedua jalur sintesis pada kisi yang makin besar membutuhkan seluruh urutan itu (operator, pengelompokan, encoding, circuit, pass manager) diulang per ukuran, jadi sebaiknya dibungkus sekali saja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collecting both metrics across a range of lattice sizes and plotting them against the lattice edge makes the difference plain:\n"
msgstr "Mengumpulkan kedua metrik pada berbagai ukuran kisi dan memplotnya terhadap sisi kisi membuat perbedaannya jelas:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit depth is 24 and constant from $3 \\times 3$ to $8 \\times 8$ (that is 18 qubits up to 128), while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) applied to the identically encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly with the lattice edge, from 47 to 92. The gate count grows under both, since there are $O(N)$ terms to apply either way; what the flow sets remove is the growth in how many layers those gates occupy.\n"
msgstr "Depth dua-qubit-nya 24 dan konstan dari $3 \\times 3$ sampai $8 \\times 8$ (yaitu 18 qubit sampai 128), sedangkan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) yang diterapkan pada Hamiltonian dengan encoding identik tumbuh linear terhadap sisi kisi, dari 47 sampai 92. Jumlah gate tumbuh pada keduanya, karena ada $O(N)$ suku yang harus diterapkan bagaimanapun; yang dihilangkan flow set adalah pertumbuhan jumlah layer yang ditempati gate-gate itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The budget splits into 16 for the hopping and eight for the interaction:\n"
msgstr "Anggarannya terbagi menjadi 16 untuk hopping dan delapan untuk interaksi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each of the four flow sets costs $2 + 2$ two-qubit layers: its Clifford going in and the inverse coming out, both depth two by construction, with only single-qubit rotations in between. That is $4 \\times 4 = 16$, which is the figure Ref. <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) quotes, since it counts the hopping terms only. Setting $U = 0$ in the code above reproduces it.\n"
msgstr "Masing-masing dari empat flow set memakan $2 + 2$ layer dua-qubit: Clifford-nya saat masuk dan inversnya saat keluar, keduanya berdepth dua menurut konstruksi, dengan hanya rotasi single-qubit di antaranya. Itu $4 \\times 4 = 16$, angka yang dikutip Ref. <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), karena ia hanya menghitung suku hopping. Mengatur $U = 0$ pada kode di atas mereproduksinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagonal group adds the remaining eight. Its `Rzz` gates pack into four layers, and each `Rzz` decomposes into two `CX` gates around a single-qubit rotation, so $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Four layers is optimal: on a square lattice, the interaction reaches only nearest neighbors, so every interior site carries four `Rzz` gates (one per bond) and can take part in only one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Kelompok diagonal menambah delapan sisanya. Gate `Rzz`-nya terkemas dalam empat layer, dan setiap `Rzz` terdekomposisi menjadi dua gate `CX` mengapit satu rotasi single-qubit, jadi $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Empat layer adalah yang optimal: pada kisi persegi, interaksi hanya menjangkau tetangga terdekat, jadi setiap site interior membawa empat gate `Rzz` (satu per ikatan) dan hanya bisa ikut serta dalam satu pada satu waktu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing in either sum refers to the lattice size, which is the whole point.\n"
msgstr "Tidak ada dalam kedua penjumlahan itu yang merujuk ukuran kisi, dan itulah intinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Verify the circuit {#8-verify-the-circuit}"
msgstr "8. Verifikasi circuit {#8-verify-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The flow-set synthesis and [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) describe the same Trotter step of the same encoded Hamiltonian, so their unitaries must agree up to a global phase. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Sintesis flow set dan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) menggambarkan langkah Trotter yang sama dari Hamiltonian ter-encode yang sama, jadi unitary keduanya harus sama hingga fase global. Statevector acak mendeteksi ketidakcocokan apa pun jauh lebih murah daripada membangun unitary penuh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both circuits are decomposed down to one- and two-qubit gates *before* being applied to a state. Left un-decomposed, each high-level `Evolution` instruction forces [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) to build its full $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$ dense operator; decomposing first lets it apply gates one at a time instead, which is several hundred times faster here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua circuit didekomposisi menjadi gate satu- dan dua-qubit *sebelum* diterapkan ke sebuah state. Kalau dibiarkan tak terdekomposisi, setiap instruksi `Evolution` tingkat tinggi memaksa [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) membangun operator dense penuhnya yang berukuran $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$; dengan mendekomposisi dulu, ia bisa menerapkan gate satu per satu, yang di sini beberapa ratus kali lebih cepat.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the same phase across several random states is what closes the gap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua bagian pemeriksaan itu penting. Overlap bermodulus satu pada satu state perlu tetapi belum cukup: sintesis yang salah pada fase yang bergantung pada state tetap akan terlihat. Mensyaratkan fase yang sama pada beberapa state acak-lah yang menutup celahnya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-stabilizers\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Verify the physics on the stabilizer subspace {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"
msgstr "9. Verifikasi fisikanya pada subruang stabilizer {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the two-dimensional wrinkle. In 1D, the encoding was an isometry, and comparing spectra against a Jordan-Wigner reference was enough. VC is not an isometry: it uses $2N$ qubits for $N$ modes, so a $2^{2N}$-dimensional space holds a $2^N$-dimensional physical one. This is generic to local encodings in two dimensions (the surplus qubits are constrained by local commuting symmetries, one per plaquette <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) and it means the encoded Hamiltonian represents the fermionic one faithfully only on the joint $+1$ eigenspace of those constraints.\n"
msgstr "Inilah kerumitan dua dimensinya. Di 1D, encoding-nya adalah isometri, dan membandingkan spektrum terhadap referensi Jordan-Wigner sudah cukup. VC bukan isometri: ia memakai $2N$ qubit untuk $N$ mode, sehingga ruang berdimensi $2^{2N}$ memuat ruang fisik berdimensi $2^N$. Ini umum terjadi pada encoding lokal di dua dimensi (qubit berlebih dibatasi oleh simetri komut lokal, satu per plakuet <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) dan artinya Hamiltonian ter-encode mewakili yang fermionik secara setia hanya pada eigenspace $+1$ gabungan dari kendala-kendala itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The word **stabilizer** does double duty in this subject, and the two meanings are unrelated. Ref.   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) uses it for the commuting transfer operators of a flow set, which form a stabilizer group that the Cliffords of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) diagonalize (a compilation device, and the sense meant everywhere above). This section uses it in the error-correction sense: operators whose $+1$ eigenspace is the physical subspace. Ref.   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) explicitly flags this collision and sets the second meaning aside; the plaquette constraints below are a property of the VC encoding   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), not a result of the flow-set framework.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Peringatan\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Kata **stabilizer** punya dua fungsi dalam topik ini, dan kedua maknanya tidak berhubungan. Ref.   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) memakainya untuk operator transfer komut dari sebuah flow set, yang membentuk grup stabilizer yang didiagonalkan oleh Clifford dari [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) (sebuah alat kompilasi, dan makna yang dimaksud di seluruh bagian atas). Bagian ini memakainya dalam makna koreksi error: operator yang eigenspace $+1$-nya adalah subruang fisik. Ref.   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) secara eksplisit menandai tabrakan ini dan menyisihkan makna kedua; kendala plakuet di bawah adalah properti encoding VC   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), bukan hasil dari kerangka flow set.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The generators are constructed here rather than quoted: one per square face, and each is simply the encoded **edge**-operator loop around that face.\n"
msgstr "Generator-generatornya dibangun di sini, bukan dikutip: satu per muka persegi, dan masing-masing tidak lain adalah loop operator **sisi** ter-encode di sekeliling muka itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edge operators are the natural object for this. A closed loop of them is a symmetry of any particle-number-conserving Hamiltonian, whereas the corresponding loop of transfer operators is not: the two differ by a vertex operator on each bond’s source site,\n"
msgstr "Operator sisi adalah objek yang alami untuk ini. Loop tertutup darinya adalah simetri dari Hamiltonian apa pun yang menjaga jumlah partikel, sedangkan loop operator transfer yang bersesuaian bukan: keduanya berbeda oleh operator vertex pada site sumber setiap ikatan,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Around a closed loop every site is the source of exactly one bond, so the loop collects one $V_j$ per site, which is the **local parity** of the plaquette’s four sites. That local parity is what makes the difference: the Hamiltonian hops particles across the plaquette boundary, so it conserves only the *global* parity. The bare transfer loop therefore fails to commute with it, while the edge loop (which carries the parity factor) commutes.\n"
msgstr "Di sekeliling loop tertutup, setiap site menjadi sumber tepat satu ikatan, jadi loop mengumpulkan satu $V_j$ per site, yaitu **paritas lokal** dari empat site plakuet. Paritas lokal itulah yang membuat perbedaan: Hamiltonian memindahkan partikel melintasi batas plakuet, jadi ia hanya menjaga paritas *global*. Loop transfer polos karena itu tidak komut dengannya, sedangkan loop sisi (yang membawa faktor paritas) komut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since the encoding is defined on transfer operators, mapping an edge operator needs the relation above. That is a five-line callback, and it slots into [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") exactly as `vc_action` slots into [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"
msgstr "Karena encoding didefinisikan pada operator transfer, memetakan operator sisi membutuhkan relasi di atas. Itu callback lima baris, dan ia masuk ke [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") persis seperti `vc_action` masuk ke [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each generator has weight $6$, spread over two of its plaquette’s physical qubits and four ancillas. They are involutory and commute with the encoded Hamiltonian, so the physical subspace is preserved by the dynamics. Both properties are statements about operators, so they are checked symbolically on the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) algebra, no $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$ matrices required:\n"
msgstr "Setiap generator berbobot $6$, tersebar pada dua qubit fisik plakuetnya dan empat ancilla. Mereka involutif dan komut dengan Hamiltonian ter-encode, jadi subruang fisik terjaga oleh dinamikanya. Kedua properti ini adalah pernyataan tentang operator, jadi diperiksa secara simbolik pada aljabar [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), tanpa perlu matriks $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the stabilizers in hand, the comparison needs no basis correspondence, because $V_j = Z_j$ means the occupations live on the same physical qubits in both pictures. So: write a product state directly on the physical qubits with the ancillas in $|0\\rangle$, project it onto the stabilizer subspace, evolve with the encoded Hamiltonian, and read the site densities $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ off both sides.\n"
msgstr "Dengan stabilizer di tangan, perbandingan tidak butuh korespondensi basis, karena $V_j = Z_j$ berarti okupansi berada pada qubit fisik yang sama di kedua gambaran. Jadi: tulis state produk langsung pada qubit fisik dengan ancilla di $|0\\rangle$, proyeksikan ke subruang stabilizer, evolusikan dengan Hamiltonian ter-encode, dan baca densitas site $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ dari kedua sisi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every step here stays at the level of a vector. The projector is applied one $(1 + S)/2$ factor at a time instead of being multiplied out, and the time evolution uses [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), which computes $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ without ever forming $e^{-iHt}$. Since the encoded Hamiltonian is a sparse $2^{2N}$-dimensional operator, that distinction is what keeps this section cheap.\n"
msgstr "Setiap langkah di sini tetap di level vektor. Proyektor diterapkan satu faktor $(1 + S)/2$ sekali waktu alih-alih dikalikan penuh, dan evolusi waktu memakai [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), yang menghitung $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ tanpa pernah membentuk $e^{-iHt}$. Karena Hamiltonian ter-encode adalah operator sparse berdimensi $2^{2N}$, perbedaan itulah yang membuat bagian ini tetap murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those are the encoded densities; they match the Jordan-Wigner reference to machine precision, on a lattice whose encoding is faithful only after projection.\n"
msgstr "Itulah densitas ter-encode; cocok dengan referensi Jordan-Wigner hingga presisi mesin, pada kisi yang encoding-nya setia hanya setelah proyeksi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"measure-the-trotter-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "10. Measure the Trotter convergence {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"
msgstr "10. Mengukur konvergensi Trotter {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Step 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) established that the two syntheses agree with each other, which is a statement about equivalence rather than accuracy: both describe the same single Trotter step, so both carry the same Trotter error. Measuring that error needs an exact reference, and step 9 just built one.\n"
msgstr "[Langkah 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) menetapkan bahwa kedua sintesis sepakat satu sama lain, yang merupakan pernyataan tentang ekuivalensi, bukan akurasi: keduanya menggambarkan langkah Trotter tunggal yang sama, jadi keduanya membawa error Trotter yang sama. Mengukur error itu membutuhkan referensi eksak, dan langkah 9 baru saja membangunnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The step count comes from [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), the fermionic counterpart of the qubit-level formula used as the baseline earlier. Applied to the whole grouped operator before the decomposition, its repetition cycles between the four flow sets and the diagonal group instead of within any one of them:\n"
msgstr "Jumlah langkah berasal dari [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), padanan fermionik dari rumus level qubit yang dipakai sebagai baseline tadi. Diterapkan pada seluruh operator berkelompok sebelum dekomposisi, pengulangannya bersiklus di antara empat flow set dan kelompok diagonal, bukan di dalam salah satunya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fidelity climbs monotonically toward one as the steps shorten, which is the behavior a product formula must show. Shortening the steps is only one of the two knobs; [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") trades them against each other at a higher order, as [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) measures.\n"
msgstr "Fidelity naik secara monoton menuju satu seiring langkah memendek, yang merupakan perilaku yang harus ditunjukkan product formula. Memperpendek langkah hanyalah satu dari dua tuas; [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") mempertukarkan keduanya pada orde yang lebih tinggi, seperti yang diukur di [Sintesis gate Evolution dalam ruang fermionik](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single step of this Hamiltonian at $t = 1$ is a poor approximation (the four hopping sets and the interaction do not commute) so the first row is far from one, and that is the point: the convergence is what confirms the construction, not any single row.\n"
msgstr "Satu langkah Hamiltonian ini pada $t = 1$ adalah aproksimasi yang buruk (keempat set hopping dan interaksi tidak komut) jadi baris pertama jauh dari satu, dan itulah intinya: konvergensinya yang mengonfirmasi konstruksi ini, bukan satu baris mana pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor of the schedule spans every mode of this lattice, so narrowing a factor to its support is a no-op here and the absolute qubit indices `FlowSetSynthesis` matches on are unchanged. A synthesis written for an operator whose groups touch only part of the register would have to account for that relabeling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Setiap faktor dari jadwal ini mencakup setiap mode kisi ini, jadi mempersempit sebuah faktor ke support-nya tidak berpengaruh di sini dan indeks qubit absolut yang dicocokkan `FlowSetSynthesis` tidak berubah. Sintesis yang ditulis untuk operator yang kelompoknya hanya menyentuh sebagian register harus memperhitungkan pelabelan ulang itu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Yang perlu dibawa pulang {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two dimensions changes the bookkeeping, not the recipe.** Every ingredient from the 1D guide carries over unmodified: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") for the grouping, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for the mismatched register, and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") to wire it into the transpiler. What grew is the number of cases inside each.\n"
msgstr "**Dua dimensi mengubah pembukuannya, bukan resepnya.** Setiap bahan dari panduan 1D terbawa tanpa perubahan: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") untuk pengelompokan, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") untuk encoding, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") untuk register yang tak cocok, dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") untuk menyambungkannya ke transpiler. Yang bertambah adalah jumlah kasus di dalam masing-masing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Disjointness is what makes 2D constant-depth.** A flow set decomposes into vertex-disjoint lines, so its Cliffords are emitted in parallel and share two two-qubit layers no matter how large the lattice is. Four flow sets and a diagonal group then give a fixed budget: here $16$ for the four flow sets plus $8$ for the diagonal interaction group.\n"
msgstr "**Keterputusan-lah yang membuat 2D berdepth konstan.** Sebuah flow set terurai menjadi garis-garis vertex-disjoint, jadi Clifford-nya dikeluarkan secara paralel dan berbagi dua layer dua-qubit sebesar apa pun kisinya. Empat flow set dan satu kelompok diagonal lalu memberi anggaran tetap: di sini $16$ untuk keempat flow set ditambah $8$ untuk kelompok interaksi diagonal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Each orientation is its own Pauli shape.** $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ turns `XXZ` into `YYZ` and `XYXY` into `YXXY`, so the four flow sets need four Cliffords. Assuming that one Clifford covers both orientations of an axis is the easiest way to get a 2D flow-set synthesis wrong.\n"
msgstr "**Setiap orientasi adalah bentuk Pauli-nya sendiri.** $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ mengubah `XXZ` menjadi `YYZ` dan `XYXY` menjadi `YXXY`, jadi keempat flow set membutuhkan empat Clifford. Mengira satu Clifford mencakup kedua orientasi sebuah sumbu adalah cara termudah untuk salah dalam sintesis flow set 2D.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Read supports off the conjugation.** In 1D, one `CZ` brickwork gives the images in closed form. In 2D there is no such formula, and column lines have non-contiguous ancillas, so a hand-derived guess at where each term lands is fragile. Conjugating and inspecting the result costs one [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) construction and cannot be wrong; it also means an equally valid Clifford that lands the terms elsewhere keeps working.\n"
msgstr "**Baca support dari konjugasi.** Di 1D, satu brickwork `CZ` memberikan citra dalam bentuk tertutup. Di 2D tidak ada rumus seperti itu, dan garis kolom punya ancilla yang tidak berurutan, jadi tebakan hasil turunan tangan tentang di mana setiap suku mendarat itu rapuh. Melakukan konjugasi dan memeriksa hasilnya hanya memerlukan satu konstruksi [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) dan tidak bisa salah; itu juga berarti Clifford yang sama validnya yang mendaratkan suku di tempat lain tetap bekerja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Let the grouping do the sorting.** Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself per group, the synthesis is handed one flow set at a time and never has to re-derive the partition: it reads one Pauli shape off the first term and picks the matching Clifford. Assuming that, and raising when it does not hold, is what keeps `synthesize` short.\n"
msgstr "**Biarkan pengelompokan yang mengurutkan.** Karena [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") memecah dirinya per kelompok, sintesis diberi satu flow set sekali waktu dan tidak pernah perlu menurunkan ulang partisinya: ia membaca satu bentuk Pauli dari suku pertama dan memilih Clifford yang cocok. Mengasumsikan itu, dan melempar error saat tidak berlaku, itulah yang menjaga `synthesize` tetap pendek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The step count sits above the split.** The synthesis here sees one flow set per gate, so it cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that in fermionic space, before the decomposition, which is what makes a convergence test possible at all.\n"
msgstr "**Jumlah langkah berada di atas pemisahan.** Sintesis di sini melihat satu flow set per gate, jadi ia tidak bisa membagi evolusi ke seluruh set. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") melakukannya di ruang fermionik, sebelum dekomposisi, yang membuat uji konvergensi mungkin dilakukan sama sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify on the subspace.** A $2N$-qubit encoding of $N$ modes is faithful only where the stabilizers say it is. Because VC keeps $V_j = Z_j$, the cheapest reliable check is to project a product state and compare densities: no intertwiner and no spectral matching, which is unreliable when the restricted Hamiltonian is degenerate.\n"
msgstr "**Verifikasi pada subruang.** Encoding $2N$ qubit untuk $N$ mode hanya setia di tempat stabilizer mengatakan demikian. Karena VC mempertahankan $V_j = Z_j$, pemeriksaan andal yang paling murah adalah memproyeksikan state produk dan membandingkan densitas: tanpa intertwiner dan tanpa pencocokan spektral, yang tidak andal ketika Hamiltonian terbatasnya degenerate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The encoded Hamiltonian commutes with the stabilizers, so the projection only has to be applied to the initial state. The evolution preserves the subspace by itself. On real hardware this is also what makes the encoding useful as an error-detection resource: the stabilizers can be measured.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hamiltonian ter-encode komut dengan stabilizer, jadi proyeksi hanya perlu diterapkan pada state awal. Evolusinya menjaga subruang dengan sendirinya. Pada hardware nyata, inilah juga yang membuat encoding berguna sebagai sumber daya deteksi error: stabilizer bisa diukur.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next {#next}"
msgstr "Selanjutnya {#next}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend what is above, and both are changes of ingredient rather than of method. The first is the encoding: Verstraete-Cirac was chosen here because Ref. <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives its diagonalizing Cliffords in closed form, but Derby-Klassen spends one ancilla per odd plaquette instead of one per site, for a qubit-to-mode ratio of $3/2$ rather than $2$. Its transfer operators have different Pauli shapes, so a port amounts to rewriting the encoding function of [step 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) and finding the Clifford for each new shape; the grouping, the layout, and the synthesis scaffolding carry over untouched.\n"
msgstr "Dua arah memperluas apa yang ada di atas, dan keduanya adalah perubahan bahan, bukan metode. Yang pertama adalah encoding: Verstraete-Cirac dipilih di sini karena Ref. <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) memberikan Clifford pendiagonalnya dalam bentuk tertutup, tetapi Derby-Klassen memakai satu ancilla per plakuet ganjil alih-alih satu per site, untuk rasio qubit-ke-mode $3/2$ dan bukan $2$. Operator transfernya punya bentuk Pauli yang berbeda, jadi memindahkannya berarti menulis ulang fungsi encoding dari [langkah 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) dan mencari Clifford untuk setiap bentuk baru; pengelompokan, layout, dan perancah sintesisnya terbawa tanpa tersentuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second is the lattice itself. Everything here assumes open boundaries and a single fermionic species. Periodic boundaries close each line into a cycle: the arrows still all commute, since each meets the next head-to-tail, but the two Clifford shapes of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) are built for a line with endpoints. A cycle of $L$ sites carries $L$ bonds per orientation where a line carries $L - 1$, so the wrap-around bond has no place in the construction and needs handling of its own. A spinful model is easier: it doubles the register and adds on-site interaction terms to the diagonal group, without touching the flow sets. Neither disturbs the constant-depth argument, but both change the bookkeeping, which, as the first takeaway says, is the part that two dimensions makes bigger.\n"
msgstr "Yang kedua adalah kisinya sendiri. Semua di sini mengasumsikan batas terbuka dan satu spesies fermionik. Batas periodik menutup setiap garis menjadi siklus: panahnya masih semua komut, karena masing-masing bertemu berikutnya secara head-to-tail, tetapi kedua bentuk Clifford dari [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) dibangun untuk garis yang punya ujung. Siklus dengan $L$ site punya $L$ ikatan per orientasi sedangkan garis punya $L - 1$, jadi ikatan wrap-around tidak punya tempat dalam konstruksi dan perlu penanganan tersendiri. Model spinful lebih mudah: ia menggandakan register dan menambah suku interaksi on-site ke kelompok diagonal, tanpa menyentuh flow set. Tidak satu pun mengganggu argumen depth konstan, tetapi keduanya mengubah pembukuan, yang, seperti dikatakan poin pertama, adalah bagian yang diperbesar oleh dua dimensi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Hardware connectivity is not addressed here.** Every circuit above is built on an abstract register where any pair of qubits can interact, and the reported depths are counted in that setting. Real devices have a restricted coupling map, and mapping this encoding onto one is a substantial problem in its own right: the VC register is a $2N$-qubit graph whose gates run between a site and its own ancilla, between neighboring sites and between neighboring ancillas, so a layout has to keep all three kinds of pairs adjacent simultaneously. If it cannot, the transpiler inserts `SWAP` gates, and the layers they add are what the constant-depth construction was buying back. Ref.   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) likewise quotes its depth figure under an assumed square connectivity graph with `CX` as the only native entangler. Finding good layouts and routing strategies for local encodings on a given device topology is beyond this guide’s scope.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Konektivitas hardware tidak dibahas di sini.** Setiap circuit di atas dibangun pada register abstrak di mana sembarang pasangan qubit bisa berinteraksi, dan depth yang dilaporkan dihitung dalam kondisi itu. Perangkat nyata punya coupling map terbatas, dan memetakan encoding ini ke sana adalah masalah besar tersendiri: register VC adalah graf $2N$ qubit yang gate-nya berjalan antara sebuah site dan ancilla-nya sendiri, antara site bertetangga dan antara ancilla bertetangga, jadi sebuah layout harus menjaga ketiga jenis pasangan itu tetap berdekatan secara bersamaan. Kalau tidak bisa, transpiler menyisipkan gate `SWAP`, dan layer yang mereka tambahkan adalah apa yang dibeli kembali oleh konstruksi depth konstan. Ref.   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) juga mengutip angka depth-nya dengan asumsi graf konektivitas persegi dan `CX` sebagai satu-satunya entangler native. Mencari layout dan strategi routing yang baik untuk encoding lokal pada topologi perangkat tertentu di luar cakupan panduan ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

